Read as: speedup > 1 means the adaptive split is faster than fixed-128.
The win is batch=1 short/medium context, where a fixed 128 leaves the
stage-1 grid below one wave (num_sms*16 = 1152 blocks on A10) and the
policy splits finer to fill it. Every other shape already fills the GPU
at 128, so the policy returns the baseline and the cell is exactly 1.0x
(coarsening an overfilled grid was measured and dropped: sign flipped
with shape, magnitude inside noise). mid_o partials are MB-scale and
consumed by the merge immediately (L2-resident), so the win is grid
occupancy, not a DRAM round-trip avoided.
